## Why This Is Asked

Telemetry quality is critical for root cause analysis and cross-service tracing; this checks practical skills for CI, instrumentation, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry integrity, trace propagation, OpenTelemetry, CI gates, canary deployments
- Error budgets and dashboards alignment
- Synthetic validation and fallback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenTelemetry middleware for trace propagation
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

function ensureTraceId(req, res, next) {
  const carrier = propagation.createExtractHeadersCarrier(req.headers);
  const ctx = propagation.extract(context.active(), carrier);

  if (!trace.getSpan(ctx).spanContext().traceId) {
    const tracer = trace.getTracer('default');
    const span = tracer.startSpan('fallback-trace');
    propagation.inject(context.active(), carrier);
  }
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure telemetry coverage and what would trigger a rollback?
- What trade-offs exist when dropping events missing trace_id?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design safe, scalable chaos experiments for multi-region, real-time systems with precise blast radius control and explicit recovery criteria. Strong answers demonstrate experience with distributed systems resilience patterns and operational maturity.

## Key Concepts

- Chaos experiments with blast radius and safety constraints
- Multi-region latency, replication lag, and data integrity
- Circuit breakers, backpressure, and local message buffering
- Canary deployments with automated rollback criteria
- Telemetry: RED metrics (Rate, Errors, Duration), p95 latency thresholds, error budgets, and distributed tracing

## Code Example

```javascript
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold, timeout) {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  recordFailure() {
    this.failures++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failures >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
      setTimeout(() => this.state = 'HALF-OPEN', this.timeout);
    }
  }

  recordSuccess() {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  canExecute() {
    return this.state !== 'OPEN';
  }
}
```

